{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jut3b1rXbs5TkEXd7H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\nDear Admissions Committee,\n\nI am writing to recommend Priya Nair for doctoral study in marine ecology. I have taught biology at Westbrook College for 17 years and have supervised about 30 senior theses. Priya is one of the three best students I have taught in that time.\n\nPriya took three courses with me and earned the top grade in a class of 28 in two of them. The work Priya did outside the classroom is even stronger evidence of readiness for a PhD.\n\nFor a senior thesis, Priya compared oyster growth at six sites in our bay over 14 months. Priya did all of the fieldwork, making about 90 trips by kayak to reach the sites through every season of the year. Many undergraduates can design a field study. Few can keep one running for more than a year without anyone checking that the trips get made. Priya found faster growth at the two sites near the salt marsh. This comes from one study period and needs to be repeated before it can be published. Still, it is a real lead, and with another season of data I expect it to become a publishable paper. Priya presented the work as a poster at a regional conference.\n\nLast summer, Priya worked as a paid field assistant at a state shellfish lab. For two weeks, Priya ran the lab's water sampling alone. The supervisor there told me he would hire Priya again.\n\nPriya has already shown the qualities that matter most in field ecology. Those qualities are sustained effort over long field seasons, reliability when working without supervision, and the ability to turn many days on the water into a clear result. I recommend Priya Nair to your program without reservation and would be glad to answer any questions.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Anne Caldwell\nDepartment of Biology\nWestbrook College\n</final_document>\n\nI didn't know Priya's pronouns, so the letter uses only her name. That's why \"Priya\" repeats more than usual. If you find out her pronouns, swapping a few of those for pronouns will make it read more smoothly.\n\nA few other notes:\n\n- **Generic or addressed:** The generic greeting works for every program, so you can send this one letter to all of them by December 1. If a program gives you a faculty contact's name, change only the greeting line.\n- **Before sending:** Add your academic title (for example, Professor of Biology) and your email or phone number under your name.\n- **The storm gap:** I didn't mention the three months of lost data at one site. \"Needs to be repeated\" already covers the study's limits. If you later learn how she handled the gap, one sentence about it would strengthen the thesis paragraph."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1037,"cache_read_input_tokens":9926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1037},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"750497fc-140d-41ca-9862-aaf26fa774f1","uuid":"5c79d79f-df3c-4ca4-ba77-36c3995d375d","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:23:07.715Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7Juspww7qF83UV5r3eH"}
